sqlite3 (the SQLite command-line shell) is built from source by BundleDock into one
statically linked executable. The executable combines the following works; the
license text of each is retained in this directory.

1. SQLite (sqlite3.c, shell.c): in the public domain. The source files state:

     The author disclaims copyright to this source code.  In place of
     a legal notice, here is a blessing:

        May you do good and not evil.
        May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
        May you share freely, never taking more than you give.

   See https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html. No license file is required.

2. linenoise (linenoise.c, line editing for an interactive terminal): BSD-2-Clause,
   Copyright (c) 2010-2014, Salvatore Sanfilippo and Copyright (c) 2010-2013,
   Pieter Noordhuis. The conditions require the copyright notice and disclaimer
   to be retained in binary form in the accompanying materials: see
   LINENOISE-LICENSE.

3. musl libc (statically linked C library): MIT, Copyright (c) 2005-2020 Rich
   Felker, et al., with the notices of the individual files it lists: see
   MUSL-COPYRIGHT.

4. Zig compiler runtime code (compiler_rt and other support code that the zig
   compiler adds to the output): MIT, Copyright (c) Zig contributors: see
   ZIG-LICENSE. The zig compiler itself is a build tool and is not shipped.

SQLite and linenoise are compiled from the pinned sources named in SOURCE. musl and
the Zig runtime come from the pinned zig archive named there.
